  "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - IIO ADC drivers;\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - PCI subsystem;\n  - VFIO drivers;\n  - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;\n  - Overlay file system;\n  - IPv6 networking;\n  - Netfilter;\n(CVE-2024-53194, CVE-2024-53214, CVE-2024-56570, CVE-2024-56779,\nCVE-2024-57849, CVE-2024-57904, CVE-2024-57929, CVE-2025-21664,\nCVE-2025-38724, CVE-2026-53131, CVE-2026-53221)\n",
  "id": "USN-8922-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in the Linux kernel.\n",
